: "ZView desktop start-up.  An ordinary /bin/sh script, run by the window"
: "server when it comes up: this file, not the server, decides what is on"
: "screen at start-up.  (Note the : lines -- Coherent's sh has no # comment.)"
:
: "Start every app in the BACKGROUND with & .  A GUI app does not exit while"
: "its window is open, so a line without & would hold this script -- and the"
: "rest of the desktop -- until the user closed that one window."
:
: "Options every GUI app understands (inc/hrapp.h):"
: "	-P <X>,<Y>	where to put the window (top-left of the frame)"
: "	-S <W>x<H>	content size, for a resizable app only"
: "	-T <title>	window title	-I <file.icn>	desktop icon"
: "	-H		start minimised to a desktop icon"
:
: "An app left out of here is not lost: the right-click desktop menu lists"
: "everything in /usr/hr/etc/apps, and any app can also be run by name from a"
: "terminal window."

: "zterm's frame is 650x403 (80x25 cells of the 8x15 terminal font + frame),"
: "so at 48,40 it spans x 48..698.  The clock's 250x268 frame goes to its"
: "right: 720..970, inside the 1024-wide screen and clear of the terminal."

/usr/hr/bin/zterm -P 48,40 &
/usr/hr/bin/zclock -P 720,40 &
